"note": "hi @shovon0203 thanks for reporting this issue.\nAfter verifying 3GPP TS 24.501 (Rel 16.14.0), it seems to me that AMF handles correctly Initial UE message since UE does not have a valid 5G NAS security context at that moment.\nPlease check `Section 4.4.6 Protection of initial NAS signalling messages (3GPP TS 24.501)`.\nThanks",
"note_html": "<p data-sourcepos=\"1:1-4:6\" dir=\"auto\">hi <a href=\"/shovon0203\" title=\"Tasnim Alam\" class=\"gfm gfm-project_member js-user-link\" data-user=\"12468\" data-original=\"@shovon0203\" data-container=\"body\" data-placement=\"top\" data-reference-type=\"user\">@shovon0203</a> thanks for reporting this issue.\nAfter verifying 3GPP TS 24.501 (Rel 16.14.0), it seems to me that AMF handles correctly Initial UE message since UE does not have a valid 5G NAS security context at that moment.\nPlease check <code data-sourcepos=\"3:14-3:91\">Section 4.4.6 Protection of initial NAS signalling messages (3GPP TS 24.501)</code>.\nThanks</p>",
"body_first_line_html": "<p>hi <a href=\"/shovon0203\" title=\"Tasnim Alam\" class=\"gfm gfm-project_member js-user-link\" data-user=\"12468\" data-reference-type=\"user\">@shovon0203</a> thanks for reporting this issue....</p>",
