"note": "Hi @tien-thinh.nguyen I checked again, and also check with other cores I tested. Let me try to clarify\n\nThe spec says, when you are sending REGISTRATION REQUEST, which means InitialUEMessage from NGAP perspective, if you don't have the 5G NAS Security Context, the REGISTRATION REQUEST message should include cleartext IE's only. (Please read (a) in the screenshot I sent in the previous message). We can not send `Capability GMM` in REGISTRATION REQUEST which is a non-cleartext IE.\n\nIn case you need to send the non-cleartextIE, what you need to do is when security context is established in SECURITY MODE COMPLETE, you add the entire REGISTRATION REQUEST message again in **NAS Message Container IE** with both cleartext and non-cleartext IEs. (Please refer to (a)(1) in the screenshot again.)\n\nI hope this help clarification. I am referring to REGISTRATION REQUEST (InitialUEMessage) not SECURITY MODE COMPLETE.\n\nFor my work, I found that Open5GS handles it and rejects the message. Please let me know if you have any questions regarding this issue.",
"note_html": "<p data-sourcepos=\"1:1-1:102\" dir=\"auto\">Hi <a href=\"/tien-thinh.nguyen\" title=\"Tien-Thinh Nguyen\" class=\"gfm gfm-project_member js-user-link\" data-user=\"409\" data-original=\"@tien-thinh.nguyen\" data-container=\"body\" data-placement=\"top\" data-reference-type=\"user\">@tien-thinh.nguyen</a> I checked again, and also check with other cores I tested. Let me try to clarify</p>\n<p data-sourcepos=\"3:1-3:379\" dir=\"auto\">The spec says, when you are sending REGISTRATION REQUEST, which means InitialUEMessage from NGAP perspective, if you don't have the 5G NAS Security Context, the REGISTRATION REQUEST message should include cleartext IE's only. (Please read (a) in the screenshot I sent in the previous message). We can not send <code data-sourcepos=\"3:311-3:326\">Capability GMM</code> in REGISTRATION REQUEST which is a non-cleartext IE.</p>\n<p data-sourcepos=\"5:1-5:311\" dir=\"auto\">In case you need to send the non-cleartextIE, what you need to do is when security context is established in SECURITY MODE COMPLETE, you add the entire REGISTRATION REQUEST message again in <strong data-sourcepos=\"5:191-5:218\">NAS Message Container IE</strong> with both cleartext and non-cleartext IEs. (Please refer to (a)(1) in the screenshot again.)</p>\n<p data-sourcepos=\"7:1-7:117\" dir=\"auto\">I hope this help clarification. I am referring to REGISTRATION REQUEST (InitialUEMessage) not SECURITY MODE COMPLETE.</p>\n<p data-sourcepos=\"9:1-9:136\" dir=\"auto\">For my work, I found that Open5GS handles it and rejects the message. Please let me know if you have any questions regarding this issue.</p>",
"body_first_line_html": "<p>Hi <a href=\"/tien-thinh.nguyen\" title=\"Tien-Thinh Nguyen\" class=\"gfm gfm-project_member js-user-link\" data-user=\"409\" data-reference-type=\"user\">@tien-thinh.nguyen</a> I checked again, and also check with other cores I tested. Let me try to clarify...</p>",
